course: dictionary
lesson: 4110
title: Glacial: icy, slow and cold
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Glacial has more than one meaning, so the clues around it tell you which one to choose. Read the whole sentence first. «During the last 2.6 million years the Earth has swung between cold glacial periods and warm interglacials.» The word cold sits right beside glacial, and warm is set against it, so glacial periods must be the cold times.
explain: A glacier is a huge mass of ice that moves slowly over land, so glacial is often linked to ice. Think of glacial valleys: valleys shaped by ice. In a story, the clue might be the weather or the mood, as in a glacial wind or a glacial look.
explain: Use the swap test. Put "very cold" in place of glacial and see if the sentence still makes sense. For «at a glacial pace», "very cold" does not fit, so the meaning must be very slow instead. Always check your meaning in the sentence before you decide.
fact: Glacial means to do with glaciers or ice, as in «glacial valleys».
fact: Glacial can also mean extremely cold, as in «glacial periods».
fact: Glacial can mean very slow, as in «at a glacial pace».
fact: Informally, glacial can describe someone who is very unfriendly and cold.
fact: An interglacial is a warmer time between glacial periods.
exercise: «The explorers camped in a glacial valley, carved out by ice over thousands of years.» What is a glacial valley? | *A valley shaped by ice | A valley full of flowers in summer | A deep cave under the sea | A hot, dry desert valley
exercise: «The room felt glacial, so Mum turned on the heating.» What does glacial mean here? | Very slow | *Extremely cold | Very loud | Made of glass
exercise: Ellie says the queue moved at a glacial pace. What does glacial mean here? | Very friendly | *Very slow | Very cold | Very bright
test: «The teacher gave me a glacial stare when I was late.» What does glacial suggest? | Very fast | Sleepy and tired | Warm and welcoming | *Cold and unfriendly
test: In «cold glacial periods» and «warm interglacials», what does the word warm tell you about the glacial periods? | They were the same as interglacials | *They were the opposite, the cold times | They were warmer than the interglacials | They were very busy times
exam: «For the last 2.6 million years Earth has swung between cold glacial periods and warmer interglacials.» What does glacial mean here? | *Icy, cold times | Happy, sunny times | Fast, busy times | Quiet, empty times
